[{"id":2836565077,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6pEoxV","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?u=24618295fece29a0bf5c850faf2555985232f5f2&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","login":"aaronfranke","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke"},"body":"Indeed, the old code is not good. To summarize, this is checking if the vectors are (anti)aligned and treating that as a special case to avoid coordinate singularities (a 180 degree arc is ambiguous which direction it rotates in). Also, the inputs to this check are normalized. Therefore, this should be using a very strict comparison only to avoid coordinate singularities, not the typical use of `CMP_EPSILON` as a way to compare with a tolerance for arbitrary inputs (though, it's also the wrong value for the intended use case: #37241).\r\n\r\nNormalizing is reasonable in the arc constructor I guess, because the calculation happens in many steps, and the result could be off near the coordinate singularities. But I'm not sure if it's needed in the axis-angle constructor... that seems like a separate fix. That constructor already requires the input axis is normalized, but maybe its tolerance is too generous for this. Does normalizing the axis also give the correct result? If so, that would be a cheaper operation than normalizing the Quaternion, but then it makes the is_normalized check useless.\r\n\r\nLooking at this in more detail, this code we currently have is silly:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nif (Math::abs(d) > ALMOST_ONE) {\r\n\tif (d >= 0) {\r\n\t\treturn; // Vectors are same.\r\n\t}\r\n\tVector3 axis = n0.get_any_perpendicular();\r\n\t// etc ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere is no reason to compute the absolute value (also we could add a comment):\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nif (d > ALMOST_ONE) {\r\n\treturn; // Vectors are same.\r\n} else if (d < -ALMOST_ONE) {\r\n\t// A 180 degree arc is ambiguous which rotation got there, so just pick one.\r\n\tVector3 axis = n0.get_any_perpendicular();\r\n\t// etc ...\r\n```","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106337#pullrequestreview-2836565077","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106337","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-05-13T12:35:03Z"},{"id":2838247689,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6pLDkJ","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","login":"TokageItLab","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106337#pullrequestreview-2838247689","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106337","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-05-13T22:13:24Z"},{"id":2847552862,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6pujVe","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"37aca09b237ee009e61574fb91082f9d55b0ad54","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","login":"lyuma","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma"},"body":"","html_url":"https://